cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use K-Bound / KGA, please cite it as below."
title: "K-Bound: When Is Label-Free Adaptation Knowable?"
abstract: >-
  K-Bound studies label-free test-time adaptation as an adapt/freeze/abstain
  decision. Over a declared rich class of binary prediction problems, it gives
  a matched-evidence impossibility result, a calibration-residual frontier for
  strict commitment, and an evidence-fibre audit floor. The practical KGA rule
  turns an interval for a predeclared scalar target into a decision. Its
  marginal false-commitment control is conditional on the stated coverage,
  sampling, and transfer assumptions; coverage of measured cell outcomes does
  not automatically certify population-risk improvement. The maintained
  implementation is the lightweight `kga` Python package.
type: software
